WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.033
-There is a lot to go over,

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.400
so let's jump in
and cover it all at once.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.400
It's time for a "News Smash."
Here we go.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.434
♪♪

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:12.501
First up, Don Jr.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.300
Today, he testified
in the Trump family's

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.567
civil fraud trial.
It was a big deal.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.067
This has been years
in the making,

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:18.868
kind of like...

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.767
new music
from the Beatles.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:24.567
They're releasing a new song
tomorrow using old recordings,

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.400
and A.I.
It's amazing.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.300
This new technology
could really change the game.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.334
Tonight was game 5
between Arizona and Texas,

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.901
featuring some of
the sport's greatest athletes.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.300
They're in peak
physical condition,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.667
mostly because
they don't eat

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:40.100
DiGiorno's new
Thanksgiving pizza.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.367
It's got turkey,
creamy gravy, potatoes,

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.267
green beans, and cheese.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.634
If you're eating one of these
on Thanksgiving,

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:49.400
clearly, your life has been
a huge disappointment.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.801
Don Jr. is hoping
that if he does a good job,

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.400
his dad will take him outside
and finally say,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.400
[ As Donald Trump ]
"Want to have a catch?"

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.000
[ Normal voice ]
The Diamondbacks and Rangers

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.567
are both trying
to win a championship,

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:01.634
and it all comes down
to who gets the outs

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:03.534
and who gets the runs.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:06.868
And if you take down
that whole pie,

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.067
you're gonna be shouting,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:11.334
"Help! I need somebody!"
or, "Get back!" you know?

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:12.901
Those are great songs.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.067
So is "Here Comes the Sun."

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.834
Don Jr. took the stand,

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.067
but you won't be able to stand
once you finish

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.133
a turkey-covered pizza.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.467
If you eat that thing,

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.100
your stomach will be
looking at you like,

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.501
"Pitch, please."

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:28.367
Both teams are trying to deliver
a title to their fans,

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.000
but it's -- it's not delivery,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.567
it's DiGiorno.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:33.734
In conclusion,

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:37.033
"Twist and Shout,"
strike three, you're out,

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.767
"Daddy, bail me out,"

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.267
gonna get gout?

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.767
This has been a "News Smash."

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.634
♪♪

